; MidiCamd -- the music through camd.library (-M gm, port/amiga/musik_camd.c):
; camd 37.14's built-in serial driver sends cluster out.0 to FS-UAE's serial
; port, captured raw (SERIAL_RAW: tools/serial_capture.py). The install has
; no songs (they come from the user's CD): the test's own, made by
; tools/zmu_test_song.py into DEV:Test/midi-songs, go into DEV:Zod/music for
; this run and out again. A 40 s bot match on orig01 in software. Then on the
; Mac: tools/zmu_midi_check.py build/autotest/MidiCamd.serial dist/Test/midi-songs
; LIMIT 600
; SERIAL_RAW
FailAt 1000
Wait 5
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/zod-#?
MakeDir >NIL: DEV:Zod/music
Copy DEV:Test/midi-songs/#?.zmu DEV:Zod/music/ QUIET
List DEV:Zod/music/#?.zmu >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== software, orig01, music through camd (-M gm) ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
; a jump as the danger levels make them: to step 1500 (past the song's
; CC7 change at 1200) once a song has played 6 s
SetEnv ZOD_MIDI_TESTJUMP 1500@6
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunZodMidi mid 40 -o -m Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig01.map
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/zod-mid.done
Type DEV:Test/zod-mid.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
UnSetEnv ZOD_MIDI_TESTJUMP
Delete >NIL: DEV:Zod/music/#?.zmu
Delete >NIL: DEV:Zod/music
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
